const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"规则可以随经济变化作出反应",en:"A rule can respond to the economy"},body:{zh:"Taylor首先澄清，规则并不等于固定不变的政策工具。利率可以按通胀和实际活动变化而调整，关键是反应具有可理解、相对稳定的结构。因此，利率发生变化不能单独证明决策是随意的，也不能把固定增速规则当作唯一形式。",en:"Taylor distinguishes systematic policy from an unchanging instrument. Interest rates may respond to inflation and activity through an understandable, reasonably stable relation. A rate change alone does not establish discretion, and constant-growth rules are not the only form of systematic policy."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~johntayl/Papers/Discretion.PDF",label:{zh:"1993年期刊版 · pp. 196–197",en:"1993 journal article · pp. 196–197"}}},{title:{zh:"有判断，不代表每次重新发明政策",en:"Judgment need not mean starting over each time"},body:{zh:"季度模型无法处理所有短期冲击，潜在产出也不能直接观测。作者因而允许在执行中使用判断，同时反对把每次决定都视为完全独立的问题。讨论规则时，需要区分长期反应方式与短期特殊情形下的操作调整。",en:"Quarterly models cannot cover every short-lived disruption, and potential output is not directly observed. The paper therefore allows judgment in implementation without treating every decision as a wholly new problem. Distinguish the durable response pattern from operations under unusual conditions."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~johntayl/Papers/Discretion.PDF",label:{zh:"1993年期刊版 · pp. 197–198",en:"1993 journal article · pp. 197–198"}}},{title:{zh:"设计、过渡与日常执行分开",en:"Separate design, transition and daily implementation"},body:{zh:"选用怎样的规则、怎样从原有制度过渡、日常怎样操作，是作者提出的三个不同问题。即使一种规则在模型比较中表现良好，也不能跳过制度过渡与实际执行；只展示一个目标利率数字，会把这些层次隐藏起来。",en:"The article separates choosing a rule, moving toward it and operating it day to day. Good performance in a model comparison does not settle transition or implementation. Displaying a single implied interest rate conceals these separate institutional and operational questions."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~johntayl/Papers/Discretion.PDF",label:{zh:"1993年期刊版 · p. 199",en:"1993 journal article · p. 199"}}},{title:{zh:"公式里的通胀与产出都有明确口径",en:"Inflation and output in the illustration have precise meanings"},body:{zh:"示例写作r＝p＋0.5y＋0.5(p－2)＋2，其中p是过去四个季度的通胀率，y是实际GDP相对趋势GDP的百分比偏离。y不是GDP增长率；把环比通胀或同比产出增速直接代入，会改变原式所回答的问题。",en:"The illustration is r = p + 0.5y + 0.5(p − 2) + 2. Here p measures inflation over the previous four quarters and y is the percentage deviation of real GDP from trend. The output gap is not GDP growth, and quarterly inflation is not the same input."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~johntayl/Papers/Discretion.PDF",label:{zh:"1993年期刊版 · p. 202 · equation (1)",en:"1993 journal article · p. 202 · equation (1)"}}},{title:{zh:"常数不是对所有时期的估计",en:"The constants are not universal estimates"},body:{zh:"当通胀处于示例中的2%目标、产出等于趋势时，公式给出的名义利率为4%。这个结果包含文中对实际均衡利率的示例性设定。它便于讨论政策反应，却不说明当前或任何国家的均衡利率都应取同一数值。",en:"At the illustrative 2 percent inflation target and trend output, the formula gives a 4 percent nominal rate. This incorporates an assumed equilibrium real rate. It makes the response mechanism easy to discuss but does not estimate the appropriate equilibrium rate for every country or period."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~johntayl/Papers/Discretion.PDF",label:{zh:"1993年期刊版 · p. 202",en:"1993 journal article · p. 202"}}},{title:{zh:"事后拟合与当时可操作性不同",en:"Historical fit differs from real-time feasibility"},body:{zh:"文章讨论了规则与历史政策路径的接近程度，也指出测量与特殊事件带来的困难。编辑建议保留每次公布的GDP、通胀与趋势估计版本，再讨论当时能否计算该规则；用今天修订后的数据画出的拟合线，不是实时决策记录。",en:"The discussion relates a rule to past policy while recognizing measurement problems and unusual events. Editorial application: retain release vintages of GDP, inflation and trend estimates. A fitted line calculated from today's revised data is not a record of what policymakers could compute then."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~johntayl/Papers/Discretion.PDF",label:{zh:"1993年期刊版 · pp. 197–198; p. 202",en:"1993 journal article · pp. 197–198; p. 202"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"这是一篇1993年的政策规则讨论。文中的美国历史示例不是当前政策立场，也不是其他经济体的推荐利率；趋势产出、通胀口径和当时可得信息会改变解释。",en:"This 1993 discussion uses a historical US illustration. It is neither current policy guidance nor a recommended rate for other economies. Trend output, inflation definitions and information available at the time affect interpretation."}};export{e as default};
